==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cōchlea||a snail}}, from {{der|en|grc|κόχλιας||a snail with a spiral shell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒk.li.ə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkoʊ.kli.ə/|/ˈkɑk.li.ə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cochleae|s}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The complex, [[spirally]] [[coil]]ed, tapered [[cavity]] of the [[inner ear]] of higher [[vertebrate]]s, which contains the {{w|organ of Corti}} and in which sound [[vibration]]s are converted into [[nerve impulse]]s.
# A [[spiral]]-shaped shell, especially that of a [[snail]].

